BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prisma-art-prize-20th-edition-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260903T142650Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Prisma Art Prize 20th Edition
DESCRIPTION:The Prisma Art Prize is an international award for painting and
  two-dimensional artistic research based in Rome. The 20th edition selects
  emerging and established artists working in painting\, drawing\, illustra
 tion\, printmaking\, and traditional mixed media for a group exhibition at
  Palazzo Merulana\, opening November 5\, 2026. Winners share an annual cas
 h fund of EUR 2\,000 distributed across quarterly calls and receive inclus
 ion in the collective catalogue plus artist interviews. Additional opportu
 nities include solo exhibition prizes and fully funded placements at partn
 er art residencies. The prize is open internationally to all living artist
 s regardless of age\, gender\, nationality\, or educational background. Th
 e submission deadline for this edition is September 10\, 2026.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Prisma Art Prize\nLocation: Rome\, Italy\nAward: EUR 2\,000 annual c
 ash fund distributed across quarterly winners\, plus group exhibition at P
 alazzo Merulana\, inclusion in the collective catalogue\, artist interview
 s\, and eligibility for solo show prizes (Isorrophia Gallery\, Pallavicini
 -Dettori) and partner art residencies (Dar Meso\, Casacon\, Osservatorioma
 ree) EUR 34 entry fee for 1 to 3 artworks\, plus EUR 5 for each additional
  artwork up to a maximum of 8\nDuration: Group exhibition runs November 5 
 to 8\, 2026\n\nMore: https://www.prismaartprize.com/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.prismaartprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rome\, Italy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:siap-major-individual-artists-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260903T142650Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260721
SUMMARY:Deadline: SIAP: Major Individual Artists Award 2026/27 (Arts Counci
 l NI)
DESCRIPTION:The Major Individual Artists award\, part of Arts Council NI's 
 National Lottery Support for Individual Artists Programme (SIAP)\, funds e
 xtended or ambitious work by established artists\, covering specific proje
 cts\, specialised research\, personal artistic development\, and materials
 /equipment. AMOUNT: four awards of up to GBP 15\,000 each in 2026/27. ELIG
 IBILITY: established artists across all disciplines with national/internat
 ional recognition who have not previously received a major award\; academi
 cs and postgraduate artists are eligible if the project costs do not relat
 e to their institutional work or studies. Applicants must contact the rele
 vant artform officer before submission (by 10 July 2026)\; applications wi
 thout this prior contact are ineligible. No application fee. The online ap
 plication system closes precisely at the deadline and applicants must rece
 ive a confirmation email to verify successful submission. Deadline: Monday
  20 July 2026\, 12:00 noon.\n\nOrganisation: Arts Council of Northern Irel
 and\nLocation: Northern Ireland\, United Kingdom. Applicants must be based
  in Northern Ireland.\nAward: Up to GBP 15\,000 per award\; four awards av
 ailable in 2026/27. Funded through the National Lottery Support for Indivi
 dual Artists Programme (SIAP).\nDuration: Supports specific projects\, spe
 cialised research\, personal artistic development and materials/equipment.
  Activity duration not specified.\n\nMore: https://artscouncil-ni.org/fund
 ing-for-individuals/major-individual-artists?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artscouncil-ni.org/funding-for-individuals/major-individual-art
 ists?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Northern Ireland\, United Kingdom. Applicants must be based in Nor
 thern Ireland.
END:VEVENT
